1
00:00:22,697 --> 00:00:27,081
[SPEAKER_01]: This is just a small section in the Majjhima Nikaya 77.

2
00:00:27,861 --> 00:00:30,544
[SPEAKER_01]: This is the ten kasiṇas.

3
00:00:32,145 --> 00:00:36,388
[SPEAKER_01]: It says, I have proclaimed to my disciples the way to develop the ten kasiṇas.

4
00:00:37,509 --> 00:00:43,835
[SPEAKER_01]: One contemplates the earth kasiṇa, above, below, across, undivided and immeasurable.

5
00:00:47,382 --> 00:00:47,882
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, that's it.

6
00:00:47,902 --> 00:00:48,703
[SPEAKER_00]: Just do the first one.

7
00:00:48,823 --> 00:00:49,063
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

8
00:00:49,483 --> 00:00:56,506
[SPEAKER_01]: And thereby, many disciples of mine abide having reached the perfection and consummation of direct knowledge.

9
00:00:56,686 --> 00:01:09,132
[SPEAKER_01]: So, there's earth, water, fire, air, colors, blue, yellow, red, white, space, inconsciousness, kasiṇa.

10
00:01:09,672 --> 00:01:10,293
[SPEAKER_00]: Kasiṇa, yeah.

11
00:01:10,853 --> 00:01:13,354
[SPEAKER_00]: Kasiṇa literally means totality.

12
00:01:16,042 --> 00:01:18,663
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the meaning of the word kasiṇa.

13
00:01:19,303 --> 00:01:21,203
[SPEAKER_00]: And I think even in Sanskrit, it's the same.

14
00:01:21,703 --> 00:01:24,024
[SPEAKER_00]: The totality, the extent, something.

15
00:01:24,844 --> 00:01:27,965
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it only occurs in, I think, a couple of the suttas.

16
00:01:28,985 --> 00:01:34,006
[SPEAKER_00]: So, I think it was mostly, like, later interpretations, kind of took on the whole practice.

17
00:01:34,467 --> 00:01:41,488
[SPEAKER_00]: And today, when people hear kasiṇa, they think about staring at the clay disks, or balls filled with water.

18
00:01:41,868 --> 00:01:43,849
[SPEAKER_00]: But even the Buddha himself says, you contemplate.

19
00:01:44,578 --> 00:01:46,500
[SPEAKER_00]: You develop, you establish your mind upon it.

20
00:01:47,041 --> 00:02:01,956
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's like establishing your mind upon a certain greater extent, the greater totality, from the totality that your mind dwells on to day-to-day level, which is pretty much totality of sensuality, totality of ill-will, and so on.

21
00:02:02,697 --> 00:02:16,764
[SPEAKER_00]: So, when we talk about developing, eh... discerning the greater context peripherally and then maintaining that in your mind through your own sati and mindfulness, not forgetting it, that's already practicing that established mind upon a better totality.

22
00:02:16,804 --> 00:02:26,929
[SPEAKER_00]: Because totality means it unifies whether you are turning left, right, forward, backward, up, down, doesn't matter which direction you take, it's all within certain totality.

23
00:02:28,962 --> 00:02:31,004
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's why I'm broken immeasurable.

24
00:02:31,644 --> 00:02:33,246
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm broken by your choices.

25
00:02:33,266 --> 00:02:35,128
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm broken by your directions and so on.

26
00:02:36,329 --> 00:02:46,878
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if your mind is established, like, for example, in terms of the context that people can relate to, establish your mind upon the context of sense restraint.

27
00:02:48,360 --> 00:02:49,481
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it doesn't matter then.

28
00:02:50,282 --> 00:03:03,308
[SPEAKER_00]: If you want the sensuality, if you don't want sensuality, if you're barely restraining, if you're unsuccessful in your restraint, the value, the totality of the value of sense restraint remains there, held up by you.

29
00:03:04,509 --> 00:03:14,454
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you still have at least a chance, then, to return to it and start, well, and align your behavior correctly to that, to that totality of that value.

30
00:03:14,694 --> 00:03:15,414
[SPEAKER_00]: The context.

31
00:03:15,494 --> 00:03:16,435
[SPEAKER_00]: The context, exactly.

32
00:03:17,697 --> 00:03:30,166
[SPEAKER_00]: It's the worst if you abandon the totality of the value of sense restraint, and then, even if you don't necessarily engage with sensuality, you're not valuing freedom from it, and you will... thus, you will never make sufficient effort to free yourself from it.

33
00:03:31,767 --> 00:03:44,697
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you maintain that totality as unbroken value, even if you necess... like, imperfect in your sense restraint in the beginning, you can eventually perfect it, because the totality remains there as an anchor point, as a reference point.

34
00:03:46,530 --> 00:03:58,197
[SPEAKER_00]: So that's why, similarly, in other suttas, when the Buddha said, the monk who is withdrawn from village, from the crowd, lives in seclusion, solitary life in the forest, his mind establishes himself upon the perceptions of the forest.

35
00:03:58,837 --> 00:04:07,883
[SPEAKER_00]: And he recognizes any perceptions that would come on account of inferior village life, that would bother somebody, cannot bother me, because my mind is established upon the perception of the forest.

36
00:04:07,923 --> 00:04:08,703
[SPEAKER_00]: That's where I dwell.

37
00:04:09,304 --> 00:04:12,686
[SPEAKER_00]: But if something were to happen to the forest, I would be disturbed.

38
00:04:13,581 --> 00:04:18,064
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if somebody comes and starts cutting trees and destroying that forest, his perceptions would then go.

39
00:04:18,504 --> 00:04:21,526
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then, his mind would not be established because the totality is gone.

40
00:04:22,826 --> 00:04:25,308
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then, he recognizes that liability.

41
00:04:25,368 --> 00:04:27,189
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then, he reflects thus.

42
00:04:27,229 --> 00:04:31,732
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, what if I were to establish my mind upon even a greater totality that cannot be destroyed easily?

43
00:04:32,652 --> 00:04:33,593
[SPEAKER_00]: The totality of earth.

44
00:04:34,493 --> 00:04:40,837
[SPEAKER_00]: Because earth is the totality that's in common to the forest and the village and in between and the city, wherever you might be.

45
00:04:42,066 --> 00:04:46,490
[SPEAKER_00]: But the problem for people, like, is when you hear this, it's just too abstract to begin with.

46
00:04:46,570 --> 00:04:48,291
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, the idea of worth.

47
00:04:48,311 --> 00:04:50,833
[SPEAKER_00]: Because that idea doesn't stand for anything in their experience.

48
00:04:51,094 --> 00:04:58,680
[SPEAKER_00]: But that's because their experience hasn't been cultivated sufficiently enough, so that they can discern the element of worth within their experience.

49
00:04:59,301 --> 00:05:10,090
[SPEAKER_00]: And when I say cultivated sufficiently enough, means unbroken sīla developed sufficiently enough, sensory strength dedicated to sufficient enough, mindfulness cultivated sufficiently enough, right views developed sufficiently enough.

50
00:05:11,708 --> 00:05:23,035
[SPEAKER_00]: Otherwise, it will be just an abstraction that you will then sort of mystify and fantasize and equate with staring at a clay ball somehow, like, will take your mind into the magical dimension of the totality of earth.

51
00:05:23,636 --> 00:05:23,736
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

52
00:05:23,776 --> 00:05:32,181
[SPEAKER_00]: You contemplate the extent of earth, the extent of solid, which is in common to me, you, village, mountains, everything.

53
00:05:33,042 --> 00:05:34,062
[SPEAKER_00]: And it's there.

54
00:05:34,363 --> 00:05:41,067
[SPEAKER_00]: The factual, the facticity of your body, if seen rightly, reveals the element of earth, the great earth.

55
00:05:43,258 --> 00:05:50,146
[SPEAKER_00]: You've seen rightly the element of water, the totality, not the actual, physical, particular thing you focus on.

56
00:05:50,887 --> 00:05:55,833
[SPEAKER_00]: So, all these totalities are on the level of peripheral and even more peripheral, if your mind can take it.

57
00:05:57,175 --> 00:06:06,566
[SPEAKER_00]: And the atmoskāsina, the most refined kāsina, as the Buddha would say, is the one of consciousness, which is the ultimate peripheral of the negative presence, basically.

58
00:06:06,586 --> 00:06:07,126
[SPEAKER_01]: Negative, yeah.

59
00:06:07,286 --> 00:06:07,386
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

60
00:06:07,426 --> 00:06:16,757
[SPEAKER_00]: So, there's nothing substantial to consciousness, but even that can be discerned by the mind that has developed to such an extent of that peripheral perception, so to speak.

61
00:06:18,685 --> 00:06:20,105
[SPEAKER_00]: But it's the same beginning.

62
00:06:20,145 --> 00:06:27,968
[SPEAKER_00]: That context that we talk about peripherally, that's the direction of any samādhi, any jhāna, any mind development, any casino establishment.

63
00:06:28,948 --> 00:06:35,870
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's why if you cultivate it, you abandon anything inferior that your mind would be focusing on and picking on, and nothing inferior can bother you.

64
00:06:37,177 --> 00:06:40,918
[SPEAKER_00]: And if you want to actually... maybe here's an example that can illustrate this.

65
00:06:41,479 --> 00:06:42,559
[SPEAKER_00]: Think about it like this.

66
00:06:42,599 --> 00:06:46,941
[SPEAKER_00]: You live in the village or the city and you have your day-to-day worries and happiness and so on.

67
00:06:47,601 --> 00:06:48,821
[SPEAKER_00]: That's your life revolves around it.

68
00:06:48,861 --> 00:06:51,042
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't really see the greater totality.

69
00:06:51,382 --> 00:07:01,606
[SPEAKER_00]: And suddenly, you find out on the news there is a massive comet heading and it's gonna... there's a good chance it might wipe the entire planet Earth.

70
00:07:03,026 --> 00:07:15,315
[SPEAKER_00]: The greater totality than the one you live in, specifically where you're focusing and attending and choosing, how quickly would all of your village worries disappear and got replaced by a greater worry?

71
00:07:16,914 --> 00:07:23,879
[SPEAKER_00]: The totality of... and that's exactly the practice.

72
00:07:24,780 --> 00:07:34,568
[SPEAKER_00]: You want to upgrade your totality, not through focusing and staring at various things that you might believe represent on, by actually contemplating and discerning it as already there.

73
00:07:36,250 --> 00:07:44,757
[SPEAKER_00]: The totality of experience in the village or city or home or lay life or whatever else is within the totality of an enduring earth.

74
00:07:46,137 --> 00:07:46,537
[SPEAKER_00]: Already.

75
00:07:49,700 --> 00:07:52,623
[SPEAKER_00]: So, what if I were to scare you on account of that totality?

76
00:07:52,783 --> 00:07:55,105
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, everything inferior would stop bothering you.

77
00:07:56,366 --> 00:07:58,108
[SPEAKER_00]: Because you would get replaced by that bother.

78
00:07:58,588 --> 00:08:03,973
[SPEAKER_00]: But what if you were to then overcome the fear in regard to the totality of earth?

79
00:08:04,894 --> 00:08:08,977
[SPEAKER_00]: How could you then possibly be afraid on account of anything that comes from the village?

80
00:08:09,678 --> 00:08:11,500
[SPEAKER_00]: Because you don't even care what happens to the earth.

81
00:08:12,608 --> 00:08:15,849
[SPEAKER_00]: If that comment hits it or not, you're equanimous on that level.

82
00:08:16,842 --> 00:08:19,444
[SPEAKER_00]: Nothing in video that comes through your senses can bother you anymore.

83
00:08:20,165 --> 00:08:21,106
[SPEAKER_00]: You have surmounted it.

84
00:08:21,566 --> 00:08:22,367
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's what Buddha said.

85
00:08:22,387 --> 00:08:28,853
[SPEAKER_00]: Even a putujana can discern these totalities and use them to abandon sensuality and so on.

86
00:08:29,333 --> 00:08:35,378
[SPEAKER_00]: What they cannot see, without a right view, is how to relate rightly to that totality.

87
00:08:35,859 --> 00:08:37,120
[SPEAKER_00]: That is useful to abandon.

88
00:08:37,140 --> 00:08:43,925
[SPEAKER_00]: That's like sometimes when people even like, you know, like have a have a notion of God or a divine and they use it to transcend this world.

89
00:08:44,706 --> 00:08:53,710
[SPEAKER_00]: You know, the sensuality and everything else, because... but the relationship between them and the totality of God, or whatever they call it, that's... has no understanding.

90
00:08:53,810 --> 00:08:56,552
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why they're still putujan, they're still liable to rebirth and everything else.

91
00:08:57,455 --> 00:09:14,667
[SPEAKER_00]: But then the Buddha said, but the target that teaches not just the totality that you can find and use to abandon inferior things that might bother you, as in upgrade your context, even as a lay person that's not interested in practice, you'll be more beneficial to upgrade your context and not just be absorbed and narrowed down to what's right in front of you.

92
00:09:15,968 --> 00:09:17,890
[SPEAKER_00]: Find a greater totality and maintain your mind on it.

93
00:09:19,388 --> 00:09:27,273
[SPEAKER_00]: But the Tāgata teaches, then, the understanding, the gratification in regard to totality, the danger, the escape.

94
00:09:28,274 --> 00:09:36,140
[SPEAKER_00]: Basically, the Buddha used the same description as he used for, like, abandoning centrality and other unwholesome states, how to abandon the casinos.

95
00:09:37,420 --> 00:09:38,601
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's what differentiated him.

96
00:09:38,621 --> 00:09:43,145
[SPEAKER_00]: He said, like, a man might establish himself upon the element of earth,

97
00:09:44,262 --> 00:09:47,365
[SPEAKER_00]: And, eh... because of that, he would abandon everything inferior to that.

98
00:09:47,825 --> 00:09:49,707
[SPEAKER_00]: Because he cultivates his mind on that level.

99
00:09:49,847 --> 00:09:51,168
[SPEAKER_00]: That's a good cultivation.

100
00:09:51,188 --> 00:09:53,150
[SPEAKER_00]: Not necessarily wisdom of the right view.

101
00:09:53,230 --> 00:09:55,211
[SPEAKER_00]: But, obviously, he's abandoning lots of dust.

102
00:09:55,271 --> 00:09:59,075
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if he were to hear the Buddha's teaching, he wouldn't need much of an instruction.

103
00:09:59,635 --> 00:10:12,329
[SPEAKER_00]: And that teaching would be, now, the way you abandon everything inferior, understood it as impermanent, unsatisfactory, turn the same reflection to that Earth because of which you abandon everything inferior, to that totality of Earth.

104
00:10:12,989 --> 00:10:17,314
[SPEAKER_00]: Remove your emotional connection to the, I need this Earth in order to be alive.

105
00:10:17,634 --> 00:10:19,176
[SPEAKER_00]: Become equanimous on that level.

106
00:10:20,970 --> 00:10:29,157
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, you would have understood the extent of the gratification in earth, the danger in earth, the escape in earth, and the path that leads the way to escape the earth.

107
00:10:29,778 --> 00:10:33,822
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, he goes on to describe the same principle for all the ten casinos.

108
00:10:34,382 --> 00:10:39,186
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it doesn't matter how peripherally your mind can, like, is developed or can develop.

109
00:10:39,547 --> 00:10:43,831
[SPEAKER_00]: What matters is to keep, basically, rehearsing and drilling the same principle.

110
00:10:44,662 --> 00:10:45,882
[SPEAKER_00]: Discern a greater totality.

111
00:10:45,942 --> 00:10:47,242
[SPEAKER_00]: Develop a greater context.

112
00:10:48,063 --> 00:10:55,444
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, even maraṇasati, in a way, mindfulness of death, has a unifying totality to everything you experience in this life.

113
00:10:55,464 --> 00:11:00,445
[SPEAKER_00]: It's basically practice of casino, even if it's not specifically the topic of the of the casino.

114
00:11:02,505 --> 00:11:11,426
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you were to take up a context, cultivate it, and then that context in itself, see it as a reason against your will, not in your control.

115
00:11:11,447 --> 00:11:13,947
[SPEAKER_00]: You have no say in it, if it comes or goes or disappears.

116
00:11:14,922 --> 00:11:21,962
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you use it to abandon your attachment and your infatuation with objects of your senses, concerns of your senses.

117
00:11:23,198 --> 00:11:34,321
[SPEAKER_00]: You know, one of the prerequisites for entering jhāna is basically abandoning concern and worry in regard to the world, in regard to basically the sense objects.

118
00:11:34,721 --> 00:11:42,423
[SPEAKER_00]: You need to have been withdrawn first, sufficiently enough, long enough, and then the mind will start discerning this greater totality.

119
00:11:42,483 --> 00:11:45,243
[SPEAKER_00]: So, jhāna is another form of totality practice.

120
00:11:45,783 --> 00:11:52,225
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, your mind establishes upon greater totality, that in itself is free from greed, aversion, delusion, and it's wholesome.

121
00:11:53,836 --> 00:11:57,478
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's why puthujjana cannot attain jhānas as well, without the right view.

122
00:11:57,518 --> 00:12:01,361
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't need the right view to establish your mind in that principle of that totality.

123
00:12:02,442 --> 00:12:07,245
[SPEAKER_00]: But you need a form of establishment of your mind in the principle of totality in order to get the right view.

124
00:12:09,237 --> 00:12:15,304
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, some people will need more of it, some people will need less of it, depending on how, you know, quick and well-versed your mind is.

125
00:12:16,024 --> 00:12:19,008
[SPEAKER_00]: But, nevertheless, some form of samādhi, in that sense, is needed.

126
00:12:19,088 --> 00:12:24,153
[SPEAKER_00]: Like citta samādhi... cittanimitta is already a form of... it's a precursor to samādhi.

127
00:12:24,173 --> 00:12:26,275
[SPEAKER_01]: It's already a form of samādhi from Kuntujana's point of view.

128
00:12:26,295 --> 00:12:27,637
[SPEAKER_01]: Composing a greater context.

129
00:12:27,697 --> 00:12:28,037
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

130
00:12:28,077 --> 00:12:29,118
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's another totality.

131
00:12:29,719 --> 00:12:30,640
[SPEAKER_00]: Presence of the mind.

132
00:12:31,581 --> 00:12:38,647
[SPEAKER_00]: The mood is always there, regardless of how you specifically feel, or what you're specifically doing, or what you might be doing, what you're worried, what you want to do.

133
00:12:38,707 --> 00:12:41,489
[SPEAKER_00]: There is a certain container of the mood always enduring.

134
00:12:42,129 --> 00:12:46,293
[SPEAKER_00]: So you recognize, it doesn't matter if the mood is good, or bad, or neutral.

135
00:12:47,373 --> 00:12:48,995
[SPEAKER_00]: The weight of the mood is there.

136
00:12:49,255 --> 00:12:50,396
[SPEAKER_00]: That becomes your totality.

137
00:12:50,936 --> 00:12:53,418
[SPEAKER_00]: That becomes your context, that now you're maintaining.

138
00:12:53,838 --> 00:12:58,682
[SPEAKER_00]: And by maintaining the clarity in regard to it, you're basically discerning the characteristics of that mood.

139
00:12:58,742 --> 00:12:59,443
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, it endures.

140
00:13:02,603 --> 00:13:03,403
[SPEAKER_00]: You're not doing it.

141
00:13:03,423 --> 00:13:04,144
[SPEAKER_00]: You're not maintaining it.

142
00:13:04,164 --> 00:13:04,944
[SPEAKER_00]: You're liable to it.

143
00:13:05,024 --> 00:13:06,685
[SPEAKER_00]: In the same sense, the weather endures.

144
00:13:08,287 --> 00:13:15,271
[SPEAKER_00]: It affects the directions and so on, but neither of that needs to be the basis for you being affected and burdened by it.

145
00:13:15,832 --> 00:13:23,917
[SPEAKER_00]: The only time you're burdened by it is when your mind falls from that totality and gets absorbed into things that are being pressured by the mood, for example.

146
00:13:27,135 --> 00:13:30,198
[SPEAKER_00]: So, element of earth means the element, the element of solid.

147
00:13:30,218 --> 00:13:37,485
[SPEAKER_00]: The greater totality that partakes in, doesn't matter how specific and particular things are, or how general they are.

148
00:13:38,205 --> 00:13:41,368
[SPEAKER_00]: The earth is there, enduring, as a necessary basis.

149
00:13:41,408 --> 00:13:45,552
[SPEAKER_00]: The consciousness is there, enduring, as a necessary basis.

150
00:13:45,632 --> 00:13:49,916
[SPEAKER_00]: Practically speaking, the feeling is there, enduring, as a necessary basis.

151
00:13:49,936 --> 00:13:52,979
[SPEAKER_00]: That's when other suttas, they would have said, feeling is the point of converging.

152
00:13:54,354 --> 00:13:56,656
[SPEAKER_00]: The experience converges on feeling.

153
00:13:56,696 --> 00:14:00,440
[SPEAKER_00]: So, feeling is the basis for convergence of any kind.

154
00:14:00,520 --> 00:14:01,100
[SPEAKER_00]: It's framework.

155
00:14:01,280 --> 00:14:08,367
[SPEAKER_00]: When we spoke about in other talks, way of establishing mind upon the creative framework, totality, creative context, it's the same principle.

156
00:14:10,534 --> 00:14:24,445
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then, when you hear about casinos or something, you approach it as another, oh, another thing I focus on, a clay pot, or a thing filled with water, or a candle flame, and you see how far removed that is from the actual direction where casinos are.

157
00:14:25,346 --> 00:14:29,369
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you will become mystified because it's fundamentally abstract, because people cannot relate to it.

158
00:14:29,690 --> 00:14:32,192
[SPEAKER_00]: There's no basis for relating to it or getting the right idea.

159
00:14:34,159 --> 00:14:52,932
[SPEAKER_00]: But if you were to cultivate the general context, the peripheral context in regard to your current experience, and always keep that peripheral eye upon yourself, even when you are focusing on things, that's already closer to what the actual casinos are, even if you don't specifically think in terms of casinos.

160
00:14:55,474 --> 00:15:00,797
[SPEAKER_00]: And, like, that's already the nature of nimitta, nature of the sign, signs and tokens of things.

161
00:15:01,678 --> 00:15:03,079
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, even if you see a sign, stop.

162
00:15:06,795 --> 00:15:13,177
[SPEAKER_00]: The command to stop, to stop moving your body, to not cross this line, is not in the sign.

163
00:15:13,857 --> 00:15:17,718
[SPEAKER_00]: The sign is literally a shape, red and white text.

164
00:15:17,898 --> 00:15:18,898
[SPEAKER_00]: That's what you're perceiving.

165
00:15:19,438 --> 00:15:22,099
[SPEAKER_00]: Yet, you are seeing the meaning behind.

166
00:15:24,459 --> 00:15:25,039
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's what I mean.

167
00:15:25,099 --> 00:15:29,060
[SPEAKER_00]: Even when people are doing the focusing practices and so on, you still cannot escape the meaning.

168
00:15:29,180 --> 00:15:31,641
[SPEAKER_00]: You can only keep yourself oblivious to it.

169
00:15:33,822 --> 00:15:37,463
[SPEAKER_00]: Even when you're staring at things, your thoughts are there, giving the significance to that.

170
00:15:37,483 --> 00:15:38,303
[SPEAKER_00]: You're just not seeing it.

171
00:15:38,743 --> 00:15:43,044
[SPEAKER_00]: Because you think through staring or focusing, you're somehow going to have a magical release.

172
00:15:44,264 --> 00:15:45,644
[SPEAKER_00]: But that's what nimitta is already.

173
00:15:46,105 --> 00:15:49,305
[SPEAKER_00]: The meaning behind things that you perceive.

174
00:15:49,345 --> 00:15:51,126
[SPEAKER_00]: Signs and tokens, the significances.

175
00:15:51,546 --> 00:15:55,887
[SPEAKER_00]: And when the Buddha gave the simile of nimitta, it was like the cook.

176
00:15:55,907 --> 00:16:02,568
[SPEAKER_00]: Two cooks, they cook for a king, and one cooks various dishes and pays no attention to

177
00:16:03,394 --> 00:16:09,216
[SPEAKER_00]: These are basically, kind of, preferences that King will exhibit through his behavior.

178
00:16:09,276 --> 00:16:12,017
[SPEAKER_00]: He will not say, I like this, I don't like this.

179
00:16:12,637 --> 00:16:15,718
[SPEAKER_00]: But he will take six scoops of this, and only one of this.

180
00:16:16,258 --> 00:16:24,901
[SPEAKER_00]: Thus, you infer, you discern the sign, based on what you perceived, of taking this, not taking this, as meaning he likes that.

181
00:16:25,141 --> 00:16:26,642
[SPEAKER_00]: The sign that King likes that.

182
00:16:27,703 --> 00:16:29,324
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, the other doesn't discern that.

183
00:16:29,344 --> 00:16:31,484
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, the one that doesn't discern those signs gets fired.

184
00:16:31,945 --> 00:16:34,065
[SPEAKER_00]: The one that discerns it, he gets promoted.

185
00:16:34,646 --> 00:16:37,907
[SPEAKER_00]: And it's the same the monk who discerns the signs of his own mind.

186
00:16:38,207 --> 00:16:40,888
[SPEAKER_00]: When he attends to this, what signs manifest?

187
00:16:41,168 --> 00:16:42,248
[SPEAKER_00]: What meaning is shown?

188
00:16:42,328 --> 00:16:43,089
[SPEAKER_00]: What rises?

189
00:16:43,169 --> 00:16:44,849
[SPEAKER_00]: Is it sensuality, non-sensuality?

190
00:16:45,409 --> 00:16:46,810
[SPEAKER_00]: Is it ill-will or non-ill-will?

191
00:16:47,650 --> 00:16:52,132
[SPEAKER_00]: If he pays no attention to what's behind, he will not progress in the dhamma.

192
00:16:53,580 --> 00:16:56,561
[SPEAKER_00]: But even that, see, it's abstract for many people.

193
00:16:56,601 --> 00:17:03,282
[SPEAKER_00]: You say nimitta, and they think these glowing lights and flowering nimitta signs and projections and so on.

194
00:17:03,302 --> 00:17:03,442
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

195
00:17:03,622 --> 00:17:06,123
[SPEAKER_00]: It's literally signs and tokens of things.

196
00:17:06,143 --> 00:17:12,504
[SPEAKER_00]: The nimitta of the recorder, the nimitta of the book, the nimitta of the robe, what it means, what it represents, what it stands of, all are forms of nimittas.

197
00:17:13,644 --> 00:17:23,146
[SPEAKER_00]: And yes, you look at the objects that are agreeable to the eye, there are nimittas, meaning of it, that are basically enticing, pulling you towards sensuality,

198
00:17:24,785 --> 00:17:37,775
[SPEAKER_00]: But, you could also discern wider nimittas, wider significances that require a bit more effort to establish that the danger, peril, entrapment, all of the unwholesome, in the same thing you perceive in it.

199
00:17:39,136 --> 00:17:46,281
[SPEAKER_00]: Does the Buddha say, the monk who wants to practice mindfulness, he doesn't attend to the nimittas of enticing nature.

200
00:17:47,042 --> 00:17:49,864
[SPEAKER_00]: He attends to the nimittas that would result in dispassion.

201
00:17:52,103 --> 00:17:57,167
[SPEAKER_00]: And those are not these things that are kind of perceived in the... Beautiful remains beautiful.

202
00:17:57,187 --> 00:17:59,369
[SPEAKER_00]: You're still seeing the same beautiful thing.

203
00:17:59,409 --> 00:18:00,410
[SPEAKER_00]: Nimittas are not in it.

204
00:18:02,372 --> 00:18:09,478
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's already... that's already... like, I'm talking about this because that's already the principle of that... of any mind development that includes kasiṇa as well.

205
00:18:09,978 --> 00:18:16,744
[SPEAKER_00]: The nimitta, the significance of... of certain necessary basis of solidity, of earth, presence of element of earth.

206
00:18:17,264 --> 00:18:20,327
[SPEAKER_00]: If there are no things in the world, there would be no perception in the world.

207
00:18:21,904 --> 00:18:41,158
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it doesn't matter how far that... how far removed that might sound, abstractly, it's still the most, like, obvious fact, even, like, if your body is not there, as this sort of semi-solid lump, you would not be able to think, perceive, feel, like, dislike, be upset, happy, and so on.

208
00:18:42,078 --> 00:18:45,401
[SPEAKER_00]: The necessity of physical body, the necessity of the element of Earth.

209
00:18:46,643 --> 00:18:55,107
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why often, basically, like rūpa, the word rūpa was used for form, matter of any kind and for the body.

210
00:18:55,887 --> 00:18:59,949
[SPEAKER_00]: Because that's your first point of matter that you experience is your own body.

211
00:19:00,009 --> 00:19:04,752
[SPEAKER_00]: Any other matter you experience is just basically experiencing the matter of your body that experience the matter.

212
00:19:06,913 --> 00:19:08,934
[SPEAKER_00]: You cannot perceive things with your eyes.

213
00:19:09,354 --> 00:19:11,395
[SPEAKER_00]: You basically perceive your eyes seeing things.

214
00:19:14,886 --> 00:19:20,409
[SPEAKER_00]: But you see, even on a day-to-day level, how much that's forgotten, lapsed from people's context.

215
00:19:21,190 --> 00:19:25,973
[SPEAKER_00]: You forget that your senses are objects in the world that you have no control over, they will wither and die.

216
00:19:27,274 --> 00:19:35,820
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you genuinely are fully absorbed in the sense objects, fully repelled by them, as if there is no basis of your senses that enables you for either of those.

217
00:19:36,515 --> 00:19:39,156
[SPEAKER_00]: So, saḷāyatana, it's already a form of totality.

218
00:19:39,616 --> 00:19:42,417
[SPEAKER_00]: And actually, yātana means that, means base, means the extent.

219
00:19:43,398 --> 00:19:46,499
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

220
00:19:47,880 --> 00:19:49,761
[SPEAKER_00]: Fields as well, sometimes was translated.

221
00:19:53,242 --> 00:20:05,007
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the practice of kasiṇa is the practice of that peripheral establishment upon things that we unify both here and there and my sense objects, my sense organs and sense objects and everything in between.

222
00:20:06,380 --> 00:20:26,610
[SPEAKER_00]: So, whether I perceive this in the city, perceive that, whether I'm happy on account of what I perceive here, or what I perceive over there, if Earth is under threat, everything would be devalued, because now I have a greater body, that unifies, includes me, and the village, and the city, and the things that I like, and things that I dislike.

223
00:20:27,916 --> 00:20:38,283
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, just abandon the worry in regard to it, but don't abandon that peripheral context, that you do depend on the randomness of the planet Earth, the winds, the change, the earthquakes, all this, all this.

224
00:20:38,423 --> 00:20:40,865
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's another reflection the Buddha gave in another sutta.

225
00:20:41,465 --> 00:20:52,453
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if this great Earth is an unchanging mountains and so on, if they are liable to change, which they are, what is to be said about this pathetic little body?

226
00:20:53,667 --> 00:21:09,013
[SPEAKER_00]: And you experience this passion through the recognition of obvious nature that you've been ignoring before, because you haven't had the context that even this great totality of earth is liable to change, and earthquakes, and shakes, and disintegration, and heat, and so on.

227
00:21:10,013 --> 00:21:10,953
[SPEAKER_00]: Destruction, basically.

228
00:21:11,454 --> 00:21:12,514
[SPEAKER_00]: Form deforms.

229
00:21:13,154 --> 00:21:14,235
[SPEAKER_01]: And I am based on that.

230
00:21:14,515 --> 00:21:15,495
[SPEAKER_00]: And you are within that.

231
00:21:15,615 --> 00:21:19,817
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if form of that great kind, great totality, deforms,

232
00:21:20,934 --> 00:21:25,975
[SPEAKER_00]: How can I have the slightest notion that I want, or I shouldn't, or I'd be affected when I do?

233
00:21:26,115 --> 00:21:26,735
[SPEAKER_00]: It's ridiculous.

234
00:21:29,336 --> 00:21:34,878
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's why the Buddha said to those monks, like, oh, would you be upset if people come and start breaking these twigs and branches around us in this woodland?

235
00:21:35,338 --> 00:21:37,638
[SPEAKER_00]: They said, no, because, you know, who gives?

236
00:21:38,078 --> 00:21:38,358
[SPEAKER_00]: Nobody.

237
00:21:38,539 --> 00:21:41,739
[SPEAKER_00]: Nobody gives any care about these things.

238
00:21:42,339 --> 00:21:43,780
[SPEAKER_00]: So you should regard your own body.

239
00:21:44,461 --> 00:21:49,443
[SPEAKER_00]: In the same sense, like, if it were to be broken, destroyed, you should not be emotionally affected.

240
00:21:49,483 --> 00:21:53,545
[SPEAKER_00]: Because, look, these Mount Himalayas are eroding.

241
00:21:53,745 --> 00:22:00,108
[SPEAKER_00]: And what is to be said about this soft, little, tiny lump of flesh?

242
00:22:01,068 --> 00:22:02,249
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, it's obvious.

243
00:22:02,949 --> 00:22:09,792
[SPEAKER_00]: The only reason why it doesn't stick with people is because they don't invest enough effort to maintain it on the level of the context.

244
00:22:11,384 --> 00:22:12,484
[SPEAKER_00]: Because it's unpleasant.

245
00:22:12,644 --> 00:22:13,345
[SPEAKER_01]: Let it endure.

246
00:22:13,565 --> 00:22:16,405
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, like, let it endure and protect it.

247
00:22:16,485 --> 00:22:17,326
[SPEAKER_00]: It's more unpleasant.

248
00:22:17,346 --> 00:22:21,307
[SPEAKER_00]: See, like, it's like simmering fire that's starting heating you up, basically, more and more.

249
00:22:21,347 --> 00:22:22,807
[SPEAKER_00]: Eventually, the heat will accumulate.

250
00:22:23,628 --> 00:22:24,488
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, you have that anxiety.

251
00:22:24,508 --> 00:22:26,048
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

252
00:22:26,088 --> 00:22:28,169
[SPEAKER_00]: What if the earth, what if the world is to disappear?

253
00:22:28,269 --> 00:22:29,029
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, it will.

254
00:22:30,009 --> 00:22:30,650
[SPEAKER_00]: You know, what if?

255
00:22:30,870 --> 00:22:31,330
[SPEAKER_00]: It will.

256
00:22:32,110 --> 00:22:38,972
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you use that concern to become equanimous in regard to that concern on that level of the element of earth, planet of earth.

257
00:22:40,010 --> 00:22:42,852
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, nothing will bother you of the inferior nature.

258
00:22:44,753 --> 00:23:04,505
[SPEAKER_00]: But it's easier to... seemingly easier, not in the long run, but on the immediate level, it's easier to not look there and not experience that anxiety, but instead, choose to focus and absorb and fully absorb yourself in the objects of your senses, with the belief that that will somehow reveal the great truth behind and that will free you.

259
00:23:05,285 --> 00:23:07,687
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's just basically, you want more of the sensuality, pretty much.

260
00:23:07,708 --> 00:23:08,789
[SPEAKER_00]: Because that's what sensuality does.

261
00:23:09,549 --> 00:23:11,351
[SPEAKER_00]: It's full absorption with the sense object.

262
00:23:11,611 --> 00:23:22,762
[SPEAKER_00]: Fully forgetting about the necessary basis of your senses, the necessary basis of your enduring pathetic little body, and all you see is the sense object, and you're fully, kind of, in passion with it.

263
00:23:23,868 --> 00:23:30,673
[SPEAKER_00]: So now, your meditation doesn't go to those sense-objects, but takes another sense-objects of staring, hearing, feeling, touching, touching.

264
00:23:30,813 --> 00:23:31,994
[SPEAKER_01]: Getting an image in the mind.

265
00:23:32,094 --> 00:23:34,376
[SPEAKER_00]: Getting images and visions in the mind.

266
00:23:34,396 --> 00:23:35,957
[SPEAKER_00]: It's like... it's the same thing.

267
00:23:36,878 --> 00:23:39,399
[SPEAKER_00]: And you're pretty much expecting, hoping for the same results.

268
00:23:39,479 --> 00:23:42,862
[SPEAKER_00]: It will result in the culmination of the great pleasure of enlightenment and nirvana.

269
00:23:45,597 --> 00:23:50,422
[SPEAKER_00]: If you want to develop kasiṇa, start developing peripheral awareness, mindfulness, context and clarity.

270
00:23:51,683 --> 00:23:52,144
[SPEAKER_00]: And you'll see.

271
00:23:52,844 --> 00:23:57,069
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, the mind will then start being established upon the greater totality.

272
00:23:57,830 --> 00:24:07,720
[SPEAKER_00]: And you extend that totality to the element of earth, element of cohesion, element of heat, element of the presence, element of space, yeah, conserve that.

273
00:24:09,046 --> 00:24:12,030
[SPEAKER_00]: That light, that would reveal any different colors, doesn't matter.

274
00:24:12,830 --> 00:24:16,455
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why, like, Sariputin, that, I don't know, Sutta... Oh, no, maybe it was Maha Moggallon, actually.

275
00:24:18,483 --> 00:24:27,446
[SPEAKER_00]: One of the top monks at the time, it was the same log in front of him, and he was seeing it as earth, as water, as fire, as air.

276
00:24:28,386 --> 00:24:29,126
[SPEAKER_01]: The same thing.

277
00:24:29,146 --> 00:24:29,807
[SPEAKER_01]: As beautiful.

278
00:24:29,987 --> 00:24:31,147
[SPEAKER_00]: As beautiful, as ugly.

279
00:24:31,327 --> 00:24:32,507
[SPEAKER_00]: It's the same thing.

280
00:24:32,847 --> 00:24:35,028
[SPEAKER_00]: That's how versed, in all these extents, he was.

281
00:24:35,068 --> 00:24:35,868
[SPEAKER_00]: He could just pick them.

282
00:24:36,288 --> 00:24:41,150
[SPEAKER_00]: He could just pick them peripherally, in regard to the same attending log that he's attending to.

283
00:24:41,890 --> 00:24:44,893
[SPEAKER_00]: Not he's looking at different things and forgetting about the law.

284
00:24:44,933 --> 00:24:46,715
[SPEAKER_00]: He's exercising there.

285
00:24:46,775 --> 00:24:49,858
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, he's basically cultivating the discernment, that he was able to...

286
00:24:49,878 --> 00:24:50,679
[SPEAKER_00]: Developing his mind.

287
00:24:50,699 --> 00:24:51,559
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

288
00:24:52,220 --> 00:25:01,208
[SPEAKER_00]: He has discerned the element of cohesion that unifies anything that appears in your experience, your feeling, your thoughts, perceptions, internally, externally, internally and externally.

